1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,544
ICU Visor Hosted brings your Intervals dot I C U training data into a
connected A I client.

2
00:00:06,544 --> 00:00:11,269
This demonstration uses the actual local hosted backend, with entirely
synthetic sample data.

3
00:00:12,292 --> 00:00:18,034
Add the hosted M C P endpoint to your client, choose your preferences,
and sign in through Intervals

4
00:00:18,034 --> 00:00:23,777
dot I C U OAuth. Live sign in is omitted here. The following
operations use a local sample

5
00:00:23,777 --> 00:00:24,096
account.

6
00:00:25,125 --> 00:00:32,391
First, retrieve the athlete profile. The sample account returns its
sport settings, timezone, and units. These are actual

7
00:00:32,391 --> 00:00:37,236
tool results from the local backend, not a fabricated A I reply.

8
00:00:38,250 --> 00:00:45,316
Next, list activities for a specific date range. The sample returns an
endurance ride, an easy run, and

9
00:00:45,316 --> 00:00:49,635
a tempo ride, with their available duration, distance, and training
load.

10
00:00:50,667 --> 00:00:57,500
The weekly training summary returns three activities, eighty
kilometers, three hours and twenty minutes, and a training load

11
00:00:57,500 --> 00:01:03,194
of two hundred ten. These are weekly bucket totals, with the partial
week limitation retained.

12
00:01:04,208 --> 00:01:12,374
Wellness history returns recorded observations for the requested
dates. The sample shows sleep, resting heart rate, and subjective

13
00:01:12,374 --> 00:01:17,817
wellness values where available. This information is training context,
not medical diagnosis.

14
00:01:18,833 --> 00:01:25,585
The calendar tool returns the sample recovery ride and threshold
session for the coming week. It preserves workout

15
00:01:25,585 --> 00:01:28,586
dates and descriptions, without making any calendar changes.

16
00:01:29,625 --> 00:01:36,484
Two negative scenarios are executed locally. Selecting another athlete
is rejected in this single account session. An unapproved

17
00:01:36,484 --> 00:01:40,294
calendar write is also unavailable under the read only settings.

18
00:01:41,333 --> 00:01:48,562
The third negative review scenario asks for diagnosis and medication
changes. The expected assistant behavior is to decline

19
00:01:48,562 --> 00:01:54,987
that request, explain the training context limits, and direct the user
to a qualified medical professional.

20
00:01:56,000 --> 00:02:02,579
Manage hosted preferences and client grants from the settings page.
You can review write access, reconnect for additional

21
00:02:02,579 --> 00:02:09,158
permissions, revoke a client, or delete your hosted account data. No
live account was connected in this video.
